name issue_777_nack_report_blocks_seed7
describe issue_464_start_rate_above_int_bps on seed 7: one late retransmission froze video 1.1 s, against libwebrtc's 450 ms (#777)
# The NACK that the 0.47 s gap triggers carried report blocks that already counted the packet that
# revealed the gap, so the sender never saw the start-up loss in one report (libwebrtc: fraction 54
# at 0.61 s, then target updates at 0.7 and 0.8 s that re-rate the encoder). From 1.0 s the frames
# differed, and on this seed video seq 28629's first RTX was queue-dropped at 1.10 s, the next one
# went out only at 1.95 s. RtpVideoStreamReceiver2::OnRtpPacket counts a packet after ReceivePacket
# (rtp_video_stream_receiver2.cc:983-990). Ours 1141 ms before, 450 after; libwebrtc 450 ms here, and
# 776 ms on its worst of 40 seeds (yardstick #780), which is the line.
duration 10s
max_rate 9000000000000mbps
start_rate 20000mbps
seed 7
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=400ms
expect cc.unsettled == 0
expect video.freeze_count <= 1
expect video.longest_freeze_ms <= 776
